      "side": 1,
      "message": "My mistake, I copied the wrong permlink. This corresponds to enabling PartitionAlloc: https://skia-perf.luci.app/t/?begin\u003d1775825831\u0026end\u003d1775825832\u0026subset\u003dall.  There are some improvements, but clicking the boxes under a \"High\" regression column should take you to a perf graph like https://skia-perf.luci.app/e/?begin\u003d1775795162\u0026enable_chart_tooltip\u003dtrue\u0026end\u003d1776796367\u0026keys\u003dX9951237b46d8da46fca26b6c0e6211a9\u0026plotSummary\u003dtrue\u0026selected\u003dcommit%3D79029%26name%3D%252Carch%253Dx86_64%252Cbench_type%253Drecording%252Cclip%253D0_0_1000_1000%252Ccompiler%253DClang%252Cconfig%253Dnonrendering%252Ccpu_or_gpu%253DCPU%252Ccpu_or_gpu_value%253DAVX2%252Cmodel%253DGolo%252Cname%253Ddesk_motionmarkpaths.skp%252Cos%253DUbuntu24.04%252Cscale%253D1%252Csource_type%253Dskp%252Csub_result%253Dmin_ms%252Ctest%253Ddesk_motionmarkpaths.skp_1600_865%252C%26tableCol%3D13%26tableRow%3D572\u0026use_titles\u003dtrue\u0026xbaroffset\u003d78915\n\nI will send these regressions to the PA maintainers you mentioned so they can see if there is anything actionable. I agree that it is valuable to test with PA enabled, since PA is what chrome will be using when it uses Skia.\n\nFor Blink, I was referring to the disabling of third_party/blink/renderer/core|platform. I am making an educated guess that everything they are doing in that directory is basically logic on top of Skia or their similar canvas APIs, so we\u0027d see similar issues as the layer below even that.\n\nSkia does have automatic performance regression detection after you land a change, unfortunately not for a pending CL (perf.skia.org is actually the originator of the new perf tools used in chromium).",
